Subject: [PATCH] spi: aspeed: select data bus width for user-mode writes

aspeed_spi_start_user() restores ASPEED_SPI_BASE, which is single-line
mode. The outer exec_op() width selection is therefore lost before the
command/address phase. Switch to the requested data width after sending
the single-line command and address, as the read path already does.

Without this transition, quad page-program sends its data on one line
despite the SPI NOR core having selected a 1-1-4 instruction.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-aspeed-smc.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-aspeed-smc.c
@@ -263,6 +263,9 @@
 	ret = aspeed_spi_send_cmd_addr(chip, op->addr.nbytes, op->addr.val, op->cmd.opcode);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto stop_user;
+	/* Command/address are single-line; select the width for data only. */
+	if (op->data.nbytes)
+		aspeed_spi_set_io_mode(chip, aspeed_spi_get_io_mode(op));
 	aspeed_spi_write_to_ahb(chip->ahb_base, op->data.buf.out, op->data.nbytes);
 stop_user:
 	aspeed_spi_stop_user(chip);
